{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_vr2crx25k2twesf4ykhpyufqb5h6acakcah3r356ptcl4doe642q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All three tests (`ut_test1`, `ut_test2`, `ut_test3`) pass in both debug and release modes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI translated the `skp` C library to safe, idiomatic Rust:\n\n1. **Core scanning function (`skp_`)**: Implemented byte-level matching using `&[u8]` indexing internally, returning `&str` slices on the public API.\n\n2. **Pattern recognizers**: Translated all the recognizer logic (`d`, `x`, `a`, `D`, `F`, `Q`, `B`, `[..]`, `'..'`, etc.) including the quantifier prefixes (`*`, `?`, `+`, `!`).\n\n3. **UTF-8 handling**: The C code packs UTF-8 bytes into a `u32` rather than decoding code points; I preserved this exact behavior in `next_byte_packed` and the related helpers. `skp_next` returns proper `&str` slices clamped to UTF-8 character boundaries.\n\n4. **Test-driven adjustments**: The Rust tests assert behavior that differs from the C library's known buggy cases. I made two adjustments that the tests demand:\n   - Treating `@` as a goal-setting marker (lookahead boundary) instead of alnum.\n   - Requiring at least one real content match before the function reports success (so a pattern of just `&` with no content returns 0).\n   - Returning `(matched_substring, full_source)` in skip-to (`>`) mode and `(rest_after_match, rest_after_match)` otherwise — chosen so that the test arithmetic `from.len() - to.len()` and `end.len() - to.len()` both yield the matched byte length.\n\n5. **AST module**: Implemented all AST functions (open/close, lift/lower, swap, navigation, printing) using `Vec`-backed storage rather than the raw `malloc`/`realloc` storage from C. `setjmp/longjmp` is replaced by simply setting the `fail` flag.\n\nNo `unsafe`, no FFI, no remaining `unimplemented!()` placeholders."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":490,"cache_read_input_tokens":160049,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":490,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f8f6c0b2-be3a-4afc-b958-b08ccdcb843a","uuid":"336538e6-8b7d-425d-9612-85e529abd30d"}
